    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="1277" n="1263" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/9–3044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Huddle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-06">December 6,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4126. Please request the Swiss Government at its discretion as to manner and
                    timing to press the German Government to investigate the matter protested in
                    Department’s 3604 of October 23, 1944, and to take appropriate disciplinary and
                    penal action against persons responsible for the abuses referred to.<anchor
                        n="59" xml:id="d814-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d814-f1" n="59" xml:id="d814-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 8438, December 30, 1944, from Bern, reported that the Department’s
                    communication had been delivered to the German Foreign Office by the Swiss
                    Legation in Berlin on December 19 (740.00116 European War/12–3044).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
